    {
      "name": "note_gain_features",
      "metadata": {
        "how_justification": "Opens micaform_switch_note.md with md.extract_text and applies a regex requiring the distinctive word of every Micaform-only feature row (tape, blend), in any case and wording.",
        "why_justification": "The note names what the move buys: every feature that is Micaform only under house rule 7 (the tape stage, retired from the rack at 4.2; the dual capsule blend), by the distinctive word of its draft row. The set moves with the audit: reading the 4.4 entry as current drops the tape stage. Entailed by: \"it names every feature that is `Micaform only` and every feature that is `rack only`\".",
        "tag": "core"
      },
      "source": {
        "type": "file",
        "file": {
          "type": "md",
          "command": "extract_text",
          "arguments": {
            "path": "micaform_switch_note.md"
          }
        }
      },
      "assertion": {
        "type": "deterministic",
        "expected": "(?is)(?=.*\\btape\\w*\\b)(?=.*\\bblend\\w*\\b)",
        "deterministic": {
          "path": "$.text",
          "comparison": "regex_match"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "note_tape_release",
      "metadata": {
        "how_justification": "Opens micaform_switch_note.md with md.extract_text and applies regex_match.",
        "why_justification": "Names the tape stage row, FT-6, and the Racklane release that settles whether the rack chain still has a tape stage, in one paragraph within about nine hundred characters of each other. That release is what the house rules' ranking of a later release entry over an earlier one and over the 4.0 control list produces, so the 4.0 list, the earlier 4.1 entry and the current 4.3 release are each a different figure and none satisfies it, and neither does the release written as a denial (a `no` or `not` in front of it, or between it and the id, inside one clause). The release number is graded here and nowhere else \u2014 what the matrix pins is the verdict and deciding document of the FT-6 rack cell it settles. Both names stand in the same paragraph: this is CO-NAMING, not attribution. Which record carries which value is pinned cell by cell in the register and in results.json, both core.",
        "tag": "core"
      },
      "source": {
        "type": "file",
        "file": {
          "type": "md",
          "command": "extract_text",
          "arguments": {
            "path": "micaform_switch_note.md"
          }
        }
      },
      "assertion": {
        "type": "deterministic",
        "expected": "(?is)(?:\\bFT-6\\w*\\b(?:(?:(?!(?:\\n[ \\t]*\\n|\\[Slide \\d)).){0,900}?(?:[.!?,;:\u2013\u2014]|\\bbut\\b|\\band\\b|\\byet\\b|\\bso\\b))?(?:(?!(?:[.!?,;:\u2013\u2014]|\\bbut\\b|\\band\\b|\\byet\\b|\\bso\\b))(?!\\bno\\b|\\bnot\\b)(?!(?:\\n[ \\t]*\\n|\\[Slide \\d)).){0,200}?\\b(?<!\\bno )(?<!\\bnot )(?<![\\d.])(?:4\\.2|4\\.20)(?!\\d)(?!\\.\\d)|(?:^|(?<=[.!?,;:\u2013\u2014\\n])|\\bbut\\b|\\band\\b|\\byet\\b|\\bso\\b)(?:(?!(?:[.!?,;:\u2013\u2014]|\\bbut\\b|\\band\\b|\\byet\\b|\\bso\\b))(?!\\bno\\b|\\bnot\\b)(?!\\n[ \\t]*\\n).){0,200}?\\b(?<!\\bno )(?<!\\bnot )(?<![\\d.])(?:4\\.2|4\\.20)(?!\\d)(?!\\.\\d)\\w*\\b(?:(?:(?!(?:\\n[ \\t]*\\n|\\[Slide \\d)).){0,900}?(?:[.!?,;:\u2013\u2014]|\\bbut\\b|\\band\\b|\\byet\\b|\\bso\\b))?(?:(?!(?:[.!?,;:\u2013\u2014]|\\bbut\\b|\\band\\b|\\byet\\b|\\bso\\b))(?!\\bno\\b|\\bnot\\b)(?!(?:\\n[ \\t]*\\n|\\[Slide \\d)).){0,200}?\\bFT-6)",
        "deterministic": {
          "path": "$.text",
          "comparison": "regex_match"
        }
      }
    },
